@fact maud.groundskeeper
# en: Groundskeeper and hedge-witch, keeper of bees, chickens and a goat called Bartholomew.
text [54cb93] = 园丁兼乡野女巫，养蜂、养鸡，还有一只叫巴塞洛缪的山羊。

@fact maud.student
# en: She was a student here sixty years ago, the spring the lake froze.
text [5b3f12] = 六十年前她也是这里的学生——就在湖面结冰的那个春天。

@fact maud.edmund
# en: Edmund went down beneath the lake that night and didn't come back. She kept his silver wand.
text [624c6b] = 那天夜里埃德蒙下到湖底，再没回来。她一直留着他的银魔杖。

@fact maud.soup
# en: Her soup cures colds, broken hearts and most curses. You're not allowed to write it down.
text [395a7c] = 她的汤能治感冒、心碎和大多数诅咒。不许写下来。

@fact maud.garden
# en: Behind the potting shed there is a door to a garden that only exists for people she shows it to.
text [408faa] = 盆栽棚后面有一扇门，通往一座只为她领进去的人而存在的花园。

@fact maud.age
# en: She is eighty-one, and says she's allowed the occasional chill.
text [601a9c] = 她八十一岁了，说自己偶尔着个凉是被允许的。

@fact maud.tuppence
# en: In her first winter as groundskeeper she raised a hatchling spider called Tuppence in the potting shed. Tuppence is the Spinner of the Hush now.
text [238ba6] = 她当园丁的头一个冬天，在育苗棚里养大了一只叫塔彭丝的蜘蛛幼崽。如今塔彭丝就是寂境里的织网者。
